Raptor @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
=================================================

Raptor: Call of the Shadows is the vertical shoot-'em-up from Mountain King
Studios and Apogee. This is skynettx's open engine for it, built for
AmigaOS 3.x on a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, with SDL 2 through GFOpenGPU.
Status: TESTING, not a release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AmiCradle or an RTG board.
- GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module in LIBS:GFOpenGPU/ from gfopenrtg's main of
  2 November 2026 or later.
- AHI for sound. GFOpenInput for pads (lowlevel.library alone gives the
  joystick port).
- The game's data (not in this archive): FILE0000.GLB and FILE0001.GLB
  from the shareware episode (1rap12.zip, RAPSW12.SHR inside it, from
  the publisher), or the full game's FILE0000.GLB to FILE0003.GLB.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive where you keep games (lha x raptor-...lha Games:), then
put the .GLB files in the Raptor drawer, beside the program. Settings
(SETUP.INI) and saved pilots go to the drawer's User drawer.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the game's icon, or from a Shell: cd to the drawer, then
  raptor (with a stack of 256 KB or more: Stack 262144).
- The game starts on a screen of its own; Alt+Return switches to a window
  and back.
- Keys: the arrow keys move, Ctrl fires, Alt fires the special weapon,
  Space changes the special weapon, Right Shift drops a mega bomb, P
  pauses, Escape opens the in-flight menu. The hangar and the menus work
  with the mouse.

Licence
-------

The engine is GPL-2.0 (LICENSE); its source is at
https://github.com/skynettx/raptor. The game data is the publisher's and
is not part of this archive: the shareware episode may be copied freely,
unmodified and without charge (VENDOR.DOC in the shareware archive). The
icons are drawn from the engine's own program icon.

